    "result_text": "All 34 tests pass \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nReplaced the string `membershipTier` with a numeric `membershipLevel` (1\u20133), scored at creation.\n\n**Scoring logic** \u2014 new function `AssignMembershipLevel`: starts at 1, +1 when an email is present, +1 when `namesakeCount` is 0, capped at 3 (level 4 reserved for tenure). Wired into the POST pipeline right after `assignNamesakeCount` (so the namesake count is set) and before `save` (so the level is persisted and available to the audit line).\n\n**Changes made:**\n- `model/Owner.java` \u2014 added persisted `membershipLevel` field with accessors.\n- `db/{h2,hsqldb,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql` \u2014 added `membership_level INTEGER` column.\n- `rest/function/owner/AssignMembershipLevel.java` \u2014 new step computing the level.\n- `officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted the `assignMembershipLevel` step.\n- `mapper/OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 removed the `membershipTier` computed mapping; `membershipLevel` now maps straight from the entity by name.\n- `rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreated.java` \u2014 the create audit line now records `membershipLevel=` instead of the tier.\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 replaced the `membershipTier` (string) response property with `membershipLevel` (integer, 1\u20133), which regenerates `OwnerDto`.\n- `AssignHouseholdSize.java` \u2014 removed the now-stale javadoc reference to the GOLD tier.\n\nThe tier's GOLD/SILVER/BRONZE behaviour is gone, and the audit line records the level (verified in the test logs, e.g. `membershipLevel=3`).",
